[{"category":"section","location":"examples/plots/#Use-with-Plots.jl","page":"Plots.jl","text":"using Plots\nusing ProudPalettes\n\nThe palettes defined in PROUD_PALETTES can be used to set colors in Plots.jl plots.\n\nFor example,\n\nx = 0:1e-2:2π\nplot(x, cos, color = PROUD_PALETTES[:rainbow][1])\nplot!(x, sin, color = PROUD_PALETTES[:rainbow][2])\nPlot{Plots.GRBackend() n=2}\n\nThey can also be used to set the palette for a whole plot. This can be simpler than setting colors one plot at a time.\n\npalette = PROUD_PALETTES[:rainbow]\np = plot(palette = palette)\n\ny = @. sin(x) - 1\nfor (i, _) in enumerate(palette)\n    plot!(x, y .+ i, ribbon = 0.4)\nend\n\np\nPlot{Plots.GRBackend() n=6}\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"Use with Plots.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/makie/#Use-with-Makie.jl","page":"Makie.jl","text":"using CairoMakie\nusing ProudPalettes\n\nThe palettes defined in PROUD_PALETTES can be used to set colors in Makie plots.\n\nFor example,\n\nx = 0:1e-2:2π\nlines(x, cos, color = PROUD_PALETTES[:rainbow][1])\nlines!(x, sin, color = PROUD_PALETTES[:rainbow][2])\n\ncurrent_figure()\nFigure()\n\nThey can also be used to set the palette for a whole plot. This can be simpler than setting colors one plot at a time.\n\np = PROUD_PALETTES[:rainbow]\n\nfig = Figure()\nax = Axis(fig[1, 1], palette = (patchcolor = p,))\n\ny = sin.(x)\nfor (i, _) in enumerate(p)\n    band!(ax, x, y .+ i, y .+ i .+ 1)\nend\n\nfig\nFigure()\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"Use with Makie.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#ProudPalettes","page":"Home","text":"Figure()\n\nProudPalettes is a Julia package providing color palettes derived from pride flags.","title":"ProudPalettes"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"#ProudPalettes.ProudPalettes","page":"Home","text":"Colour palettes\n\nFor flags composed of horizontal stripes, the colors in each array are ordered from bottom to top. This results in color bars with an intuitive order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ProudPalettes.ProudPalettes"},{"category":"constant","location":"#ProudPalettes.PROUD_PALETTES","page":"Home","text":"const PROUD_PALETTES::Dict{Symbol,Vector{Colors.RGB}}\n\nDict of RGB vectors.\n\nExamples\n\nThe available keys are\n\njulia> using ProudPalettes\n\njulia> keys(PROUD_PALETTES) |> collect |> sort\n13-element Vector{Symbol}:\n :bi\n :lesbian\n :nonbinary\n :pan\n :pride\n :pride6\n :pride7\n :pride8\n :pride_progress\n :rainbow\n :sapphic\n :sapphic5\n :trans\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"ProudPalettes.PROUD_PALETTES"}]
